Subject: Tweak: no Mega Strikes
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

SetupGameFromConfig builds each match's own copy of the gameplay settings
(mCurGameGameplayOptions), which nothing saves. With "No Mega Strikes" enabled,
both teams' Mega Strike flags of that copy are cleared after the mode rules
are applied, so cFielder::CanDoCaptainShootToScore refuses them through the
game's own check. Skillshots stay: CanDoSidekickShootToScore reads the
separate Skillshot flags (m_unk18/m_unk19), whereas the game's Classic Mode
cheat ("No Skillshots or Megastrikes") refuses both (issue #22).

Strikers 101 keeps its rules, so its Mega Strike lessons stay completable.
Its lessons are the challenges below STRIKER_CHALLENGE_MARIO, the test the
game itself uses to tell them from the Striker Challenges, which follow the
tweak. Online matches are left alone.

diff --git a/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp b/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
index d61992c..9f8512b 100644
--- a/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/GameInfo.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "Game/NetworkSession.h"
 #include "Game/TweakRegistry.h"
 #include "Game/main.h"
+#include "mscharged_tweaks.h"
 #include "NL/nlDebug.h"
 #include "NL/nlMemory.h"
 #include "NL/nlMath.h"
@@ -399,6 +400,18 @@ void GameInfoManager::SetupGameFromConfig()
         mCurGameGameplayOptions.NumGames = 1;
     }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port tweak "No Mega Strikes": this match's own settings copy, which
+    // nothing saves, for both teams. Skillshots have their own flags and stay.
+    // Strikers 101 lessons (challenges below STRIKER_CHALLENGE_MARIO) keep
+    // their rules, as do online matches.
+    if (mscharged_tweak_enabled(MSCHARGED_TWEAK_NO_MEGA_STRIKES) && !mIsInStrikers101Mode && !IsOnline()
+        && !(mCurrentMode == GM_CHALLENGE && g_pStrikerChallenge->mCurrentChallenge < STRIKER_CHALLENGE_MARIO)) {
+        mCurGameGameplayOptions.mHomeMegastrikeEnabled = false;
+        mCurGameGameplayOptions.mAwayMegastrikeEnabled = false;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (GetTweakBool("User/skipfe", false)) {
         mCurGameGameplayOptions.NumGames = 11;
     }
